[Task Description]
Define rules that tensorflow.experimental.numpy.zeros_like API parameters should satisfy. Refer to the API documentation. Particularly, there should be at least one rule to suppress each error message.

Type is encoded as an integer (index of the following list):
[bool, np.int8, np.int16, np.int32, np.int64, np.uint8, np.float16, np.float32, np.float64, np.complex64, np.complex128, str, np.dtype]

String value should be selected from the following list:
["ii", "ii->i", "i,j->ij", "bij,bjk->bik", "...ij->...ji", "bn,anm,bm->ba", "none", "sum", "max", "min", "prod", "relu", "tanh", "sigmoid", "softmax", "elu", "selu", "gelu", "swish", "softplus", "linear", "valid", "same", "causal", "channels_last", "channels_first"]

[API Documentation]
TensorFlow variant of NumPy's `zeros_like`.

Unsupported arguments: `order`, `subok`, `shape`.

See the NumPy documentation for [`numpy.zeros_like`](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.zeros_like.html).

[API Signature] a: tensor, dtype: dtype

